# docs/README.md — Required Reading Order

> **Documentation entry point.** AI must read this file first, then follow the order below.

---

## Required Reading Order

When receiving any task, AI must read in this order:

| Order | File | When needed |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `docs/project-overview.md` | Always |
| 2 | `docs/technology.md` | Always |
| 3 | `docs/core-principles-and-coding-standards/structure.md` | When creating / modifying files |
| 4 | `docs/core-principles-and-coding-standards/coding-conventions.md` | When writing logic |
| 5 | `docs/core-principles-and-coding-standards/coding-style.md` | When formatting / linting |
| 6 | `docs/core-principles-and-coding-standards/instructions-and-work-flows/` | For specific tasks |

---

## SDD Workflow

Every new feature goes through this cycle:
```
specs/features/<name>/spec.md → plan.md → tasks.md → implement → review.md → done/
```

See details at `specs/_workflow.md`.
